app_title = Background Lab
intro = Schedule a short task and check its completion count. Compare work kept in this process with work managed by the operating system.
supported = This platform supports system-scheduled background work.
unsupported = Persistent system scheduling is unavailable on this platform.
ready = Ready
schedule = Schedule once (after at least 30 seconds)
repeat = Repeat about every 15 minutes
cancel = Cancel scheduled work
scheduled = Scheduled. The system chooses when to run; battery settings and app usage can delay it.
cancelled = Schedule cancelled
run_now = Run handler now
refresh = Refresh count
diagnostic_help = Run handler now checks the Rust handler in the foreground. It does not test system scheduling.
completed = Handler completed
failed = Handler did not complete
run_count = Completed runs: { $count }
operation_error = Could not complete the operation: { $error }
in_process_help = In-process jobs run while the app stays alive. Closing the process discards them; system suspension pauses them. They do not restart the app.
in_process_schedule = Run in this process after 5 seconds
in_process_scheduled = Scheduled in this process. Keep the app open, then refresh the count after 5 seconds.
in_process_cancel = Cancel in-process work
